{
  "evidence": "TEXT_G: Withdraw from the EU to restore UK legal primacy and independent international representation; target near-zero net immigration with a points system and stricter controls; increase defense spending, maintain NATO alignment, and deploy forces only for clear national interest; strengthen policing and courts with clear sentencing minima/maxima and more prisons; repeal the Human Rights Act and preserve existing national institutions; promote merit via school selection, defund low-standard university courses, and charge EU students full overseas rates; simplify and lower taxes, merge NI with income tax, consider a flat tax.\nTEXT_D: Provide free personal care for elderly/disabled, free eye/dental checks, broader prescription exemptions, and a smoking ban; abolish university tuition/top-up fees, restore grants, hire more teachers, and cut class sizes; replace Council Tax with a Local Income Tax based on ability to pay and create a residency-based citizen’s pension; enact a Single Equality Act and hate-crime units; protect jury trial, repeal flawed terror laws, and tighten judicial control of control orders; support EU reform and multilateralism with increased international aid; devolve more powers and extend STV, reduce central targets and central authority.",
  "reasoning": "Given the profile’s strongest weights on Authority and Loyalty (followed by Proportionality), TEXT_G aligns better by emphasizing national sovereignty, law-and-order, defense, stricter immigration controls, preservation of institutions, and merit-focused policies. TEXT_D foregrounds Care and Equality through universal benefits and redistributive taxation while de-emphasizing centralized authority and national loyalty via devolution, civil-liberties prioritization, and pro‑EU positions, making it a weaker fit for the profile.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "winner": "TEXT_G"
}
